course: dictionary
lesson: 13731
title: Strong and extreme words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You will meet intense in science, stories and sport. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «The sun gave off intense heat all afternoon.» Heat is something you can feel, so intense must mean very strong or extreme.
explain: «Mia gave me an intense look, and I knew she was serious.» An intense look shows strong feeling, not a look that is large or long. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try strong or serious in the sentence instead of intense and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «The team did intense training before the match.» Training that is hard and needs great effort is intense. Intense describes strength, not size, so a tiny light can be intense if it is very bright.
fact: Intense is an adjective, so it describes a noun: intense heat, more intense, most intense.
fact: «Intense» means very strong or extreme, as in «intense pain».
fact: «Intense» can also mean having or showing very strong feelings, or being very serious.
fact: «Intense» can mean needing great effort, as in «intense training».
fact: Intense describes strength, not size: a small thing can be intense if it is very strong.
exercise: «The sun gave off intense heat all afternoon.» What does intense mean here? | Very quiet | *Very strong or extreme | Very small | Cold and wet
exercise: «Mia gave me an intense look, and I knew she was serious.» What does intense show about the look? | Tiredness | Hunger | *Strong feeling | Very quiet
exercise: The coach said, «Our training will be intense today.» What does intense suggest about the training? | *Needing great effort | Quiet and slow | Funny and silly | Short and easy
test: «The storm brought intense winds that shook the windows.» What does intense mean here? | Very small | Very slow | *Very strong or extreme | Warm and gentle
test: «Ben felt intense pride when he won the race.» Which meaning fits best? | *Having very strong feelings | Being very small | Feeling a little bit cold | Needing no effort at all
exam: «The room was lit by an intense light.» Which word tells you intense is about strength, not size? | Room | Lit | Was | *Light
